---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Playground from '../components/Playground.svelte';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import vlLang from '../grammars/vl.tmLanguage.json';

const heroSample = `use std.print;\nfunction main() { print("Hello, world!\\n"); }`;
const overviewSample = `// A complete program has one required entrypoint\nuse std.print;\nfunction main() { print("Hello, world!\\n"); }`;
const vlThemes = { light: 'github-light', dark: 'github-dark' };
---

<Base title="VL Documentation">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-5 pb-20 pt-12 sm:px-8 lg:pt-16">
    <p class="text-[0.85rem] text-muted"><a href="/docs" class="underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 hover:text-body">VL</a> / Welcome</p>
    <p class="mt-8 text-[0.95rem] font-medium text-muted">Article</p>
    <h1 class="mt-1 max-w-[20ch] text-[clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.4rem)] font-bold leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.022em] text-ink text-balance">
      A small language you can read end to end.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.65] text-body">
      An ordered, random-access compiler. VL is an expression language compiled
      by a split-crate Rust pipeline. Every stage reports through Ariadne,
      recovers per item, and lets one root cause stay one error.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[0.82rem] text-muted">VL 0.1+ | macOS 13.0+ | Linux</p>

    <div class="code-plain mt-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-decl font-mono text-[0.85rem] leading-[1.7] text-ink">
      <Code code={heroSample} lang={vlLang} themes={vlThemes} />
    </div>

    <hr class="mt-10 border-rule" />

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-[1.7rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.018em] text-ink">Overview</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[70ch] leading-[1.65]">
      VL programs are one of the most commonly read things in this repo. You use
      <code class="rounded-md bg-pill px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em] text-ink">let</code> to organize your values
      and <code class="rounded-md bg-pill px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em] text-ink">function</code> to hold
      reusable work. For example:
    </p>

    <div class="code-plain mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-plate font-mono text-[0.83rem] leading-[1.7]">
      <Code code={overviewSample} lang={vlLang} themes={vlThemes} />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-[0.9rem] text-muted">You can check and build a program from the workspace root:</p>

    <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-xl bg-plate px-5 py-4 font-mono text-[0.83rem] leading-[1.7]">
      <p>cargo run -- check examples/hello.vl</p>
      <p>cargo run -- build examples/hello.vl --out /tmp/hello.nara</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-[1.7rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.018em] text-ink">Try a line</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[70ch] leading-[1.65]">Send VL source to the hosted compiler and inspect the returned Naravm build or its diagnostics.</p>
    <div class="mt-4">
      <Playground client:load />
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-[1.7rem] font-bold tracking-[-0.018em] text-ink">Topics</h2>
    <h3 class="mt-6 text-[1.15rem] font-bold text-ink">Reading the docs</h3>
    <p class="mt-2">In addition to this page, you can start from these entry points.</p>
    <div class="mt-2">
      <p class="mt-3"><a href="/docs" class="text-link hover:underline">Documentation</a></p>
      <p class="ml-6 mt-1 text-muted">Three short chapters, front to back.</p>
      <p class="mt-3"><a href="/std" class="text-link hover:underline">std reference</a></p>
      <p class="ml-6 mt-1 text-muted">The modules and functions available to VL programs.</p>
      <p class="mt-3"><a href="/cli" class="text-link hover:underline">CLI reference</a></p>
      <p class="ml-6 mt-1 text-muted">Every subcommand of the <code class="rounded-md bg-pill px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.85em] text-ink">vl</code> driver.</p>
      <p class="mt-3"><a href="/internals" class="text-link hover:underline">Compiler internals</a></p>
      <p class="ml-6 mt-1 text-muted">The staged pipeline and the rules that keep diagnostics predictable.</p>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-[1.15rem] font-bold text-ink">For contributors</h3>
    <div class="mt-2">
      <p class="mt-3"><a href="/internals" class="text-link hover:underline">Compiler internals</a></p>
      <p class="ml-6 mt-1 text-muted">The staged pipeline, diagnostics, recovery rules, and target boundary.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
